.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan revised after the BLOCK on capability classification. Measured on 1.107.9: wrapping meta with BedrockModelProfile.from_profile moves its prompt_cache_style from none to bedrock and leaves native_structured_output False, the same capability shape as amazon.nova-pro (mistral and cohere are also bedrock style). pydantic-ai applies every bedrock_cache_* setting only when the profile flags bedrock_supports_prompt_caching/bedrock_supports_tool_caching are True (models/bedrock.py 894-895, 928, 1102-1103, 1117-1118); both are False for meta, so no cachePoint is sent. structured.native_output_stack_supported is reached only under native_structured_output (structured.py:162-163), False for meta. capabilities.py is not edited; a test pins the classification and the absence of cachePoint.","timestamp":1794465630518854001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live probe, 2026-11-11 22:58 PST: Bedrock us-west-2 via AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock, fix-seal worktree with the fix applied (uncommitted at the time, same diff as the pushed commit). PydanticAIRunner agentic run on us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0, temp repo with notes.txt, instruction to read it with read_file. Result: completed, requests=3, tool_calls=2, finish_reason=stop, provenance prompt_cache_style=bedrock; the final text quoted the file's code word (HELIOTROPE), so the tool results reached the model.\nThe first attempt with the default max_tokens (16000) was rejected by Bedrock with ValidationException 'maximum tokens you requested exceeds the model limit of 8192' -- a separate defect, filed as a found bug. The recorded run set the existing llm max_tokens=8192.","timestamp":1794466762107296001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Commit 17b45eee99d: make verify exit 0, 2026-11-11 23:04 PST to 2026-11-12 00:26 PST (21143 passed, 29 skipped; integration 218 passed, 2 skipped). RED: 6 of the 16 new tests in tests/unit/test_bedrock_vendor_profiles.py fail on the pre-fix bedrock_model.py (meta and unknown vendor cases), all 16 pass after. Two existing tests stubbed BedrockProvider without model_profile (test_bedrock_provider._Stub, test_rp04_s4_llm_runtime lambda); their stubs gained one. Pushed as Gerrit 3364; awaiting votes.","timestamp":1794472056537580001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence: Gerrit 3364 merged as 9489d225d09 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved), submitted 2026-11-12 00:57 PST.\n- AC1 RED test: tests/unit/test_bedrock_vendor_profiles.py::test_agentic_run_on_a_meta_model_completes drives the real build_bedrock_provider (only boto3.session.Session is replaced) and failed on the pre-fix tree with LLMUnavailableError naming bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition.\n- AC2 root cause: pydantic-ai 1.107.9 models/bedrock.py:519 reads profile.bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition directly; providers/bedrock.py model_profile returns a plain ModelProfile for meta and None for unknown vendors; upstream main reads it with a False default; 1.107.10 still has the direct read; rebar pins >=1.107,<2. Fixed rebar-side in build_bedrock_provider.\n- AC3 tool turn: test_agentic_run_on_a_meta_model_completes_a_tool_turn (toolUse read_file, then end_turn; the 2nd Converse call carries the toolResult with the file content).\n- AC4 live probe: recorded in the 2026-11-11 22:58 PST comment (3 requests, 2 tool calls, finish stop).\n- AC5 classification: test_formerly_plain_profiles_classify_like_other_non_caching_bedrock_vendors plus the no-cachePoint assertion in the tool-turn test.\n- AC6 every vendor: test_every_vendor_resolves_to_a_bedrock_profile_and_existing_ones_are_unchanged over 11 vendor prefixes plus an unknown one.\n- AC7 make verify exit 0 on 17b45eee99d (same tree as 9489d225d09 for the changed files), 23:04-00:26 PST.\nFound bugs filed discovered_from: saintly-creeded-gecko (default max_tokens over Maverick limit), tardy-coltish-swellfish (false cache-ineffective warning on non-caching Bedrock vendors).","timestamp":1794473888296764001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 01:05 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED (class preexisting). Gerrit 3364 merged as 9489d225d09; completion gate passed. Follow-ups filed, not worked: saintly-creeded-gecko, tardy-coltish-swellfish. Remove the wrap in src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py on the pydantic-ai upgrade that reads bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition with a default.","timestamp":1794474316832423001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794434252581100686,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dd61d487-b1e7-4cda-a4ba-2167f0b1372a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8501-0e78-cbac-4b03"},{"link_uuid":"5a88dfed-fee2-44cb-8129-b0392ec18284","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"892d-0eba-9c56-4314"}],"description":"## Observation\n\nDriving `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` through rebar's agentic runner on Bedrock fails before any request is sent. Reproduced on main 6dbf05538f7 with the pinned `pydantic-ai-slim` 1.107.9 and a scripted Converse client: `PydanticAIRunner(cfg).run(RunRequest(..., execution_mode=\"agentic\"))` raises `LLMUnavailableError: the LLM provider call failed: bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition`.\n\n## Root cause (measured)\n\n- pydantic-ai's `BedrockConverseModel._map_tool_definition` (models/bedrock.py:519 in 1.107.9) reads `self.profile.bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition` directly whenever a tool definition is `strict`.\n- `BedrockProvider.model_profile` returns a `BedrockModelProfile` for every vendor prefix except `meta` (and unknown vendors, which return `None`): `meta` maps to `_without_builtin_tools(meta_model_profile(...))`, a plain `ModelProfile`. Surveyed all 11 vendor prefixes plus an unknown one: only `meta` and the unknown case lack the field. `ModelProfile.__getattr__` raises `AttributeError(name)`, which the runner surfaces as the bare field name.\n- Upstream defect. pydantic-ai main now reads `self.profile.get('bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition', False)`; the latest 1.x release (1.107.10) still has the direct read, and rebar pins `>=1.107,<2`. So rebar must work around it.\n- rebar builds the provider in `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.build_bedrock_provider`; pydantic-ai resolves the model's profile from `provider.model_profile`, so that is the seam (rebar already overrides `model_profile` the same way for its OpenAI-compatible provider in `providers.py`).\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py`, return a `BedrockProvider` subclass whose `model_profile(name)` returns `BedrockModelProfile.from_profile(upstream or DEFAULT_PROFILE)`. For a profile that is already a `BedrockModelProfile`, `from_profile` returns an equal object (checked for anthropic, qwen, openai), so every other vendor is unchanged; for `meta` and unknown vendors it adds the Bedrock fields with their upstream defaults (`bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition=False`), so a strict tool is sent without `strict`, as pydantic-ai main does.\n2. A comment names the upstream defect and the 2.x fix so the subclass can be removed on the 2.x upgrade.\nNo config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Capability classification (measured)\n\n`capabilities._capabilities_from_profile` sets `prompt_cache_style=\"bedrock\"` when the profile exposes `bedrock_supports_prompt_caching`; its comment states the intent: a Bedrock-hosted model is `bedrock` style \"regardless of family\". Today meta is `none` only because of the same upstream gap. After the wrap, meta's capabilities equal amazon.nova-pro's shape (`bedrock` style, `native_structured_output=False`); mistral and cohere are also `bedrock` style without caching. `capabilities.py` is not edited. The 2 consumers of the `bedrock` style, checked:\n- `cache_settings_for` returns `bedrock_cache_instructions`/`bedrock_cache_tool_definitions`/`bedrock_cache_messages`. pydantic-ai 1.107.9 applies each only when the profile's `bedrock_supports_prompt_caching`/`bedrock_supports_tool_caching` is True (models/bedrock.py 894-895, 928, 1102-1103, 1117-1118); both default False for meta, so no `cachePoint` is sent.\n- `structured.native_output_stack_supported` is called only under `caps.native_structured_output` (structured.py:162-163), which is False for meta, so output routing is unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py`\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED then GREEN: the agentic runner, with a scripted Converse client (the `test_sampling_opt_in.py` pattern), completes a turn for `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0`; on the pre-fix tree it raises `LLMUnavailableError` naming `bedrock_supports_strict_tool_definition`.\n- A tool-using turn: the script returns a `toolUse` for an agentic tool, then `end_turn`; the run completes and the second Converse call carries the `toolResult`.\n- Classification: after the fix a meta model's capabilities are `bedrock` style with `native_structured_output=False`, and the agentic Converse request for meta (instructions + tools) carries no `cachePoint` block.\n- For every vendor prefix `BedrockProvider.model_profile` knows (anthropic, mistral, cohere, amazon, meta, deepseek, openai, qwen, google, minimax, nvidia) plus an unknown one, the built provider's `model_profile` is a `BedrockModelProfile`, and for vendors whose upstream profile already is one it equals upstream.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A test that fails on the pre-fix tree reproduces the error for a `us.meta.*` model through the agentic runner.\n- [x] The root cause is recorded on this ticket with evidence (upstream 1.x defect, rebar-side workaround).\n- [x] The agentic runner completes a tool-using turn for `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` in a test.\n- [x] [non-codebase] A live agentic probe of `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` on Bedrock completes, recorded as a comment.\n  provenance: environment=Bedrock us-west-2 via the frontier-bedrock profile from the fix-seal worktree; principal=frontier-bedrock IAM identity; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — one agentic run with a tool turn\n- [x] A test shows a meta model is classified `bedrock` style with no native structured output, and its agentic Converse request carries no `cachePoint`.\n- [x] Every Bedrock vendor prefix resolves to a `BedrockModelProfile`; profiles that already were one are unchanged.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-seal worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","reason":"Bedrock-profile provider"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","reason":"regression tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","892d-0eba-9c56-4314"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ee2f2f0b-aefb-4afe-a6cf-dcbdafa42d00"